WEBVTT

00:02.372 --> 00:05.273
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.643 --> 00:09.079
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.180 --> 00:12.446
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.551 --> 00:15.349
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.787 --> 00:18.916
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.025 --> 00:22.017
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.261 --> 00:23.922
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.030 --> 00:25.623
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.766 --> 00:30.830
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:35.653 --> 00:38.680
- Hello, I'm Tom Tucker.
- And I'm Diane Simmons, reporting live

00:38.791 --> 00:41.817
from the 35th annual
Quahog Veteran's Day celebration.

00:41.927 --> 00:45.955
Yes, it was 35 years ago today
that James Veteran stood up to City Hall

00:46.066 --> 00:48.591
and said,
"I demand a parade in my name."

00:48.702 --> 00:52.537
And after a heated bidding war with
Edward Memorial and Reginald Aprilfools,

00:52.640 --> 00:53.607
he got his wish.

00:53.708 --> 00:55.403
And here comes the parade!

00:55.509 --> 00:58.502
First up, a float from
the Veterans of Future Wars.

01:02.618 --> 01:05.815
And here comes whackadoo film director,
Oliver Stone.

01:05.922 --> 01:07.480
Oliver's here promoting his new movie,

01:07.590 --> 01:10.754
<i>Born on the Fifth of July,</i>

01:10.894 --> 01:14.295
which he promises will be even July-ier
than the original.

01:14.933 --> 01:17.299
A dangerously insane human being.

01:17.736 --> 01:20.865
And here comes the next float,
honoring uninjured veterans.

01:22.041 --> 01:23.065
- Yeah!
- We rock!

01:23.175 --> 01:24.972
Our wives stayed with us.

01:26.579 --> 01:28.047
- Think fast!
- We did!

01:30.617 --> 01:33.348
Mom, how come when we see these guys
on the street corner

01:33.454 --> 01:36.480
you tell me not to stare at them,
and today that's all we're doing?

01:36.591 --> 01:39.891
Because, Chris, as Americans,
we owe our lives to these veterans.

01:39.995 --> 01:42.589
Hey, look, Lois,
"The John McCain Experience."

01:47.771 --> 01:50.433
I wanna be President!

01:53.244 --> 01:56.771
Brian, I can't see.
I'm gonna try and get a little closer.

01:56.914 --> 01:58.348
Um...

01:58.450 --> 01:59.849
You shouldn't be...

01:59.951 --> 02:01.009
Um...

02:01.686 --> 02:03.210
You need to...

02:03.321 --> 02:04.379
Um...

02:04.524 --> 02:05.491
Uh...

02:06.659 --> 02:08.217
Hold on.

02:08.528 --> 02:09.620
Um...

02:09.996 --> 02:11.055
Hello?

02:11.165 --> 02:12.189
Yeah, I'm telling him.

02:16.456 --> 02:18.425
What is that?

02:18.526 --> 02:25.296
<i>And I'm proud to be an American
where at least I know I'm free</i>

02:25.401 --> 02:31.363
<i>And I won't forget the men who died
who gave that right to me</i>

02:31.608 --> 02:38.412
<i>And I'll gladly stand up next to you
and defend her still today</i>

02:39.083 --> 02:43.180
<i>'Cause there ain't no doubt I love this land</i>

02:44.189 --> 02:50.151
<i>God bless the USA</i>

02:50.630 --> 02:55.432
Oh, my God! That was beautiful!
I am proud to be an American,

02:55.536 --> 02:58.937
and I am going
to love my country like never before.

02:59.173 --> 03:01.369
Anybody wanna see my Purple Heart?

03:05.013 --> 03:08.575
<i>- We now return to
- The Broken Condom.</i>

03:10.319 --> 03:14.347
- Hey, Lois, ready to go to dinner?
- Yeah, sure. Just let me grab my purse.

03:21.065 --> 03:22.191
Okay, ready.

03:22.300 --> 03:26.635
Ooh! On second thought, I got something
I gotta do back on Krypton.

03:26.739 --> 03:28.104
I thought Krypton was destroyed.

03:28.207 --> 03:30.505
I think we should see other people.

03:31.076 --> 03:33.170
Good morning, my American family.

03:33.279 --> 03:35.076
Peter, where did you get that suit?

03:35.181 --> 03:38.014
My God, you look like
the Statue of Liberty's pimp.

03:38.652 --> 03:40.779
This is how a patriot dresses, Lois.

03:40.888 --> 03:43.755
Boy, I never knew it would feel this good
to love my country.

03:43.858 --> 03:46.293
It's like loving God or a step-parent.

03:46.395 --> 03:49.228
You never really feel them love you back,
but that's okay

03:49.331 --> 03:52.130
because they got other stuff going on,
and you understand.

03:52.235 --> 03:54.863
Peter, you do realize there's a difference
between loving America

03:54.971 --> 03:55.995
and being swept up in post-9/11 paranoia.

03:57.595 --> 04:00.928
Brian, are you suggesting that
9/11 didn't change everything?

04:01.032 --> 04:02.124
What? No, I was just...

04:02.233 --> 04:06.261
Because 9/11 changed everything, Brian.
9/11 changed everything.

04:06.372 --> 04:09.603
Peter, you didn't even know
what 9/11 was until 2004.

04:09.709 --> 04:11.904
That's not true, Brian. I remember 9/11.

04:15.515 --> 04:17.211
Must have been a woman pilot, huh?

04:21.037 --> 04:22.665
Peter, what the hell are you doing?

04:22.773 --> 04:25.833
Lois, I am doing my duty
as a patriotic American.

04:25.943 --> 04:28.104
I'm sacrificing a goat to Toby Keith.

04:28.211 --> 04:31.841
Peter, Toby Keith doesn't want to be fed.
Toby Keith wants to hunt.

04:32.050 --> 04:34.075
Hey, listen,
don't tell me what Toby Keith wants.

04:34.185 --> 04:35.210
I think I'm perfectly capable...

04:44.030 --> 04:47.694
You're all doing such a great job,
I wanted to play you a song I wrote

04:47.802 --> 04:49.861
about what America means to me.

04:49.971 --> 04:53.840
<i>When you say USA</i>

04:53.942 --> 04:56.604
<i>I just say hooray</i>

04:56.712 --> 04:58.475
<i>And if you're not from here</i>

04:59.081 --> 05:02.779
<i>God's gonna hunt you down
and give you AIDS</i>

05:02.885 --> 05:03.874
<i>USA!</i>

05:11.795 --> 05:12.922
Wow, Peter, you're really becoming
quite the patriot.

05:14.570 --> 05:18.438
You bet I am. I just had my penis
