Is there anyone here
who hasn't had a c-section?

16:31.741 --> 16:34.209
Oh, no. That boy's ball fell out of the cup.

16:34.310 --> 16:38.748
Oh, but it's okay, because the ball
is on a string and attached to the cup.

16:39.917 --> 16:43.046
You must be the Griffins.
I am Gerardo, the head groundskeeper.

16:43.155 --> 16:47.182
You must be exhausted. Come, come.
Let's get you to your new home.

16:49.328 --> 16:52.422
<i>- Hey, Seсorita!
- You got nice bread dough legs!</i>

16:52.532 --> 16:54.433
I got a blank prescription pad!

16:57.738 --> 16:59.262
See, this isn't so bad.

16:59.373 --> 17:02.969
Not so bad? We're sharing a tool shed
with seven other families.

17:09.185 --> 17:10.743
They're making the best of it.

17:14.658 --> 17:17.559
Good morning, Mr. Pewterschmidt.
It's 8:00, and I'm ready for work.

17:17.661 --> 17:18.993
Good. Have a seat.

17:19.096 --> 17:20.495
- Drink that.
- What is it?

17:20.598 --> 17:23.260
My blood.
I'm a diabetic, and I need you to test it.

17:23.367 --> 17:25.393
- Isn't that dangerous?
- I don't know. Probably.

17:25.504 --> 17:27.768
- I don't wanna.
- You work for me. Now, drink it.

17:27.873 --> 17:30.103
- No!
- Drink my diabetic blood, Peter,

17:30.209 --> 17:31.507
or you're fired.

17:34.080 --> 17:38.711
I can't believe you really did that.
That's nasty. You're nasty.

17:41.222 --> 17:44.283
<i>My VCR's still broken.
Did you remember to watch Survivor?</i>

17:44.392 --> 17:46.087
- Yes, sir.
- All right, I wanna see it.

17:46.194 --> 17:49.561
<i>Previously on Survivor,
Grace won immunity after lying to Kyle</i>

17:49.664 --> 17:52.031
- about a stomach virus.
- I've seen this. Fast forward.

17:52.134 --> 17:54.261
Credits, commercials,
Ford, Subway, Doritos,

17:54.370 --> 17:56.134
<i>Pirates of the Caribbean 4, Orbit gum.</i>

17:56.240 --> 17:58.504
<i>Hang on, go back.
I want to see that Pirates trailer.</i>

17:58.609 --> 18:02.272
In a world where pirates are gay
but Orlando Bloom isn't,

18:02.379 --> 18:03.677
<i>comes Pirates of the Caribbean 4.</i>

18:10.273 --> 18:12.173
Peter, how was your first day?

18:12.508 --> 18:15.137
Horrible! I never worked
so hard in my life.

18:15.245 --> 18:17.270
How the hell do you guys
do this every day?

18:17.381 --> 18:21.716
- Immigrant life sucks.
- But, Peter, life in America is wonderful.

18:21.819 --> 18:23.946
That is why we risk everything
to come here.

18:24.055 --> 18:27.286
I don't know, Cheech.
It seems like a lot of work for no respect.

18:27.392 --> 18:31.887
Peter, America is the land of opportunity.
There are tall buildings,

18:32.031 --> 18:38.938
<i>cheeseburgers and Fox's many hit comedy
series, including That '70s Show, and...</i>

18:43.044 --> 18:45.239
But let me ask you something.
Don't you miss your home?

18:45.346 --> 18:49.181
Of course. We come to America
for financial opportunities, Peter,

18:49.284 --> 18:54.723
but, someday, we will return to Mexico
because our heritage is rich and glorious.

18:54.824 --> 18:57.850
Wait, wait, hang on a second. Are you
saying there's more to being Mexican

18:57.961 --> 19:00.328
than working hard
and lusting after big asses?

19:00.431 --> 19:04.367
<i>There is, Peter. In fact, we are preparing
our Cinco de Mayo celebration.</i>

19:04.468 --> 19:07.370
As a Mexican,
you must experience it with us.

19:14.213 --> 19:18.412
<i>Well, kids, enjoy yourselves.
Cinco de Mayo is as Mexican as it gets.</i>

19:18.652 --> 19:23.248
Wow, this is awesome! And later, I'm
gonna go lift free weights in a parking lot!

19:24.025 --> 19:27.791
Oh, Peter, I'm so proud that you've
embraced these people as your own.

19:27.895 --> 19:30.194
You've come a long way
from hating foreigners.

19:30.299 --> 19:33.325
Well, Lois, life can surprise you
if you open your mind a little.

19:33.435 --> 19:35.266
For example, I used to hate the Japanese,

19:35.371 --> 19:37.738
<i>but then I saw Lou Diamond Phillips
in Young Guns,</i>

19:37.841 --> 19:39.138
and now I don't hate them anymore.

19:39.242 --> 19:42.211
Peter, I don't think that
Lou Diamond Phillips is Japanese.

19:42.312 --> 19:44.679
Chinese, Japanese,
dirty knees, look at these.

19:44.782 --> 19:46.477
Hey, what do you say
we get some of them burritos?

19:47.752 --> 19:52.417
<i>Oh, muсequita, I would love to feel
your mustache on my mustache.</i>

19:52.524 --> 19:55.187
Really? Well, there's a lot more body hair
where that came from.

19:55.294 --> 19:56.352
Oh, well, then no thank you.

19:58.009 --> 20:00.534
Wow, these DVD's are
only 99 cents apiece.

20:00.645 --> 20:04.377
Hey, look at some of these Spanish
translations of the movie titles.

20:04.483 --> 20:06.508
<i>Here's The 40-Year-old Virgin,</i>

20:06.619 --> 20:10.750
<i>and in Spanish, it's called
The No-Sex Man Comes to Town.</i>

20:10.857 --> 20:16.057
<i>And here's Airplane! and in Spanish,
it's called Incredible Flying Joke Bus.</i>

20:16.163 --> 20:20.464
<i>Here's Cheaper by the Dozen,
and in Spanish, it's called Small Family.</i>

20:22.771 --> 20:25.865
What the hell is going on here?
Why aren't you people working?

20:25.974 --> 20:28.000
<i>It's Cinco de Mayo, Mr. Pewterschmidt.</i>

20:28.111 --> 20:31.239
<i>Would you like to watch
My Friend Who Sticks His Penis in a Pie?</i>

20:31.347 --> 20:35.682
Look, I don't care what day it is in Mexico,
in America we work on weekdays.

20:35.786 --> 20:39.780
Now, do your jobs or I'll deport your
lazy asses back to the third world.

20:42.360 --> 20:44.123
Wait a minute, hang on, everybody.

20:44.229 --> 20:48.189
What he just said does not represent
the America that I know and love.

20:48.301 --> 20:51.236
This country used to welcome our kind
with open arms,

20:51.337 --> 20:54.307
but men like Carter Pewterschmidt
use us for cheap labor,

20:54.408 --> 20:58.573
and then try to punish us when we
demand to be treated like human beings.

20:58.680 --> 21:01.808
Well, no more!
Lmmigrants built this country,

21:01.916 --> 21:05.182
and I say it's time for us to take it back!
Who's with me?

21:06.155 --> 21:08.885
Could you say whole speech
again in Spanish?

21:12.028 --> 21:13.052
<i>We now return to</i>

21:13.163 --> 21:16.759
Gregory Peck Has Been
in That Stall for Over 45 Minutes Now.

21:28.714 --> 21:29.682
<i>Crimony.</i>

21:38.392 --> 21:39.381
<i>Ahhh!</i>

21:39.493 --> 21:44.261
<i>Finally, now I feel well enough
to visit my grandchildren.</i>

21:48.505 --> 21:50.336
What the hell is that?

21:58.850 --> 22:02.582
Get out of the way, Mr. Pewterschmidt,
we are here to take what's ours.

22:02.688 --> 22:05.657
Well, I mean, technically it's yours,
but we don't feel like you deserve it,

22:05.758 --> 22:07.954
so we're calling it ours
and taking it anyway.

22:08.061 --> 22:11.622
But, Peter, why would you want to harm
a fellow American citizen?

22:11.731 --> 22:13.962
- What?
- All I have to do is make one call

22:14.068 --> 22:17.060
to a friend of mine in Washington,
and he can push your paperwork through.

22:17.171 --> 22:19.504
You'll officially be an American citizen.

22:19.608 --> 22:23.874
Not good enough, Mr. Pewterschmidt.
I want citizenship for everyone here.

22:23.979 --> 22:25.914
Peter, you do not have to do this.

22:26.015 --> 22:30.679
Yes I do, Gerardo. This great land should
be everything to you that it is to me.

22:30.787 --> 22:33.689
A land where a man is paid
a wage he can live on.

22:33.791 --> 22:36.191
A land where we flush every time.

22:36.293 --> 22:39.730
A land where 17 miles
is not walking distance.

22:39.831 --> 22:42.231
A land where meals
are not purchased from a truck

22:42.334 --> 22:45.532
- and then eaten in a different truck.
- All right, all right, you make your point.

22:45.638 --> 22:49.574
- It's getting a little offensive.
- That's my only offer. Take it or leave it.

22:49.675 --> 22:54.340
Peter, you must go.
We will find our own way.

22:54.448 --> 22:56.382
I'll never forget you, Gerardo.

22:56.651 --> 23:00.712
Boy, I sure am gonna miss Reynaldo,
but I'm glad I'm finally an American again.

23:00.822 --> 23:02.984
Being an immigrant
is a real pain in the ass.

23:03.092 --> 23:06.755
I'm glad, too, Peter, but I did enjoy
learning about another culture.

23:06.862 --> 23:09.331
Yeah, you know, so did I.
Well, I guess everything's back to normal.

23:09.432 --> 23:12.196
<i>Well, I guess
everything's back to normal</i>

23:12.302 --> 23:13.667
Oh, man, not this guy again.

23:13.770 --> 23:15.294
<i>Oh, man, not this guy again</i>

23:16.507 --> 23:17.496
<i>Fart!</i>

23:17.497 --> 24:18.497
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru